Subject: tooltip-v2: a closing tooltip is hidden from assistive tech while it fades out

What: TooltipV2's content carries aria-hidden="true" whenever the tooltip is closed, which is
only while Kobalte keeps it mounted for its exit animation, and the open state the root and the
content read is one shown() accessor.
Why: Kobalte leaves closed content in the page as role="tooltip" for the 80 ms of
tooltipV2Out. A tooltip closed by a scroll (Kobalte's own scroll handler) starts the 300 ms
skip-delay window, so the next trigger opens at once, and for that overlap two tooltips were
exposed side by side: on a phone the settings page's scroll anchoring closed the "Cloud
workspaces" tooltip just after it opened, and the Check button's tooltip opened beside it.

